<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Quick scan' }) %>
<main id="main-content">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-shell">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="eyebrow">Local-first authorization scan</div>
        <h1>Check your local API.<br /><span>Trace access-control gaps.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">Check an authorized API with bounded requests, then move to identity-based verification when surface evidence needs context.</p>
      </div>

      <form class="url-form quick-scan-panel" action="/scans/quick" method="post">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>" />
        <div class="form-intro">
          <h2>Scan a target</h2>
          <p>GET, HEAD and OPTIONS only. No credentials or mutations.</p>
        </div>
        <label class="field-label" for="target">Target URL</label>
        <div class="url-control">
          <input id="target" name="target" type="url" inputmode="url" required
            maxlength="2048" placeholder="http://host.docker.internal:4100" autocomplete="url" />
          <button type="submit">Run quick scan</button>
        </div>
        <label class="consent">
          <input type="checkbox" name="authorized" value="yes" required />
          <span>I own this target or have explicit authorization to test it.</span>
        </label>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-grid" aria-label="Quick scan coverage">
    <article>
      <h2>Bounded by default</h2>
      <p>Strict host and port allowlists, short timeouts, blocked redirects and capped response bodies keep the first pass controlled.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Honest confidence</h2>
      <p>Heuristics remain suspected until ownership, role and policy evidence can support a stronger conclusion.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Identity-aware follow-up</h2>
      <p>Compare owner, alternate and anonymous behavior without persisting supplied credentials in reports.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
